<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's Hanil Bank '96 net falls.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's Hanil Bank '96 net falls.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>	 (in billion won unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (won)			    356   vs	 485</p>
<p>    Net				     59   vs	   80.5</p>
<p>    Profit before tax		  115   vs	   87</p>
<p>    Operating Revenue		2,236.7 vs	1,948.5</p>
<p>    Dividend (pct, par 5,000 won)    3   vs	    4</p>
<p>    Div Register			     Dec 31</p>
<p>NOTE - Hanil Bank is a leading South Korean commercial bank. It said its share capital was unchanged at 166 million shares.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5644</p>
</text>
